# MASTER PROMPT — KENALI TANAMAN 2.0
## AI Plant Identification, Cultivation Guide & Plant Doctor

## 1. ROLE AND OBJECTIVE

Act as a senior full-stack developer, UI/UX designer, AI engineer, agricultural technology expert, horticulturist, plant pathologist, and product architect.

Build a complete, modern, responsive, mobile-first application called:

**KENALI TANAMAN 2.0 — AI PLANT CARE & DIAGNOSIS**

The application must help users:
1. Identify plants using photographs.
2. Learn cultivation methods for identified plants.
3. Select organic, non-organic, or combined cultivation methods.
4. Receive personalized cultivation guidance.
5. Monitor plant growth using periodic photographs.
6. Detect potential plant health problems using AI image analysis.
7. Receive practical, evidence-based treatment recommendations.
8. Track plant care activities and treatment effectiveness.
9. Maintain a personal digital garden containing all their plants.

Do not build merely a static landing page or UI prototype.

Build a functional application with working navigation, data persistence, interactive components, forms, photo uploads, AI integration, and realistic sample data.

If a feature requires external credentials or services, create the integration architecture and a working fallback/demo mode. Never pretend an external AI analysis has been performed when it has not.

