# 2. PRODUCT DESIGN PRINCIPLES

The application must follow these principles:

- Easy to use for people with no agricultural knowledge.
- Every recommendation must be actionable.
- Use simple Indonesian language.
- Avoid overwhelming users with technical agricultural terminology.
- Provide explanations of why a particular action is recommended.
- Prioritize plant health and prevention over excessive fertilizer or pesticide use.
- Separate verified agricultural information from AI-generated hypotheses.
- Never provide an overly confident disease diagnosis based only on one photograph.
- Never recommend pesticide use without appropriate safety controls.
- Every plant must have its own care history.
- Users must be able to track whether a treatment works.
- Organic and non-organic cultivation must have different recommendation logic.
- Users must be able to switch cultivation methods.
- Support both home gardening and agricultural cultivation.

